<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Le Kha Phieu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1931–2020</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lê Khả Phiêu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Le Kha Phieu was a Vietnamese army officer and politician who served as general secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-vietnam">Communist Party of Vietnam</a> from 1997 to 2001. A former political commissar in the army, he was seen as cautious about economic reform, and his term saw the land border treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> of 1999. He was replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nong-duc-manh">Nong Duc Manh</a> in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/le-kha-phieu.jpg" alt="Le Kha Phieu" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adj · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Kha_Phieu.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
